PC Harper's Widow Lisi spent a day in  court she listened to the grim details  of her husband's last minutes alive the  couple had been married a month when he  was called to a burglary and was dragged  to his death behind a fleeing car  it happened in rural Berkshire last  summer the two officers had finished  their shift but worked close by and went  to help the suspects were towing a  stolen quad bike jurors were told it was  in a dark country lane that PC Harper  and his colleague confronted the  suspects car as the car sped off PC  Harper's feet got tangled up in the tow  rope he was dragged along for more than  a mile at speeds averaging 42 miles per  hour swung said the prosecutor like a  pendulum as the driver tried to dislodge  him the prosecutor said when at last he  became disentangled he was left with the  most awful injuries from which he died  there on the road surrounded by  colleagues who tried in vain to save him  his injuries were simply not survivable  and he could not be saved  he died totally naked apart from his  socks and boots and some shredded  remnants of the trousers he was wearing  this was a completely senseless killing  of a young police officer in the line of  duty  the officers Widow left Court as jurors  were shown police dashcam footage of the  bloody trail left by the escaping car in  the dark are Henry long 18 and 2 17-year  old boys who can't be named because of  their age they all deny murder but they  admit a plot to steal the quad bike  Henry long admits being the car driver  and has pleaded guilty to manslaughter  the prosecutor said it was a ludicrous  idea that he didn't know PC Harper was  tied to his car the three defendants  were arrested at a traveler's caravan  site later the same night the prosecutor  said long tolled brazen lies in police  interviews the others said nothing  jurors were shown police dashcam footage  of the moment the defendants car raced  off they heard PC  as fellow officer swear and radio in  I've lost my colleague Martin brunt Sky  News at the Old Bailey
 

